cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PanScript, please cite it as below, along with the tools it uses (CITATIONS.md)."
title: "PanScript: isolate-specific bacterial RNA-seq quantification across a pangenome"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dinan
    given-names: Adam
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/adamd3/PanScript"
abstract: >
  A Nextflow pipeline that quantifies gene expression in bacterial RNA-seq data
  without a single reference genome. Reads from each isolate are pseudo-aligned
  to that isolate's own gene set, and expression is merged across isolates
  through the orthologous gene groups of a Panaroo pangenome, then normalised
  with core-genome size factors.
keywords:
  - RNA-seq
  - bacteria
  - pangenome
  - transcriptomics
  - Nextflow
